        "id": "15",
        "kind": "comment",
        "config": {
          "text": "How to vary it:\n• Change the seed in the Project tab for a new tune with the same rules.\n• Turn pulses and rotation on the rhythms: 5 or 9 pulses, or a 12-step melody against the 16-step bass, which drifts and comes back around.\n• Pick another scale (dorian, blues, whole_tone) or root on both Scale Quantize nodes.\n• Set Pick a pitch's distribution to normal so the melody clusters in the middle.\n• Put a Probability between Melody rhythm and its three targets so some hits drop out.\nRandom notes can pile up into a loud moment nobody planned, so a Limiter keeps the peaks under −1 dB."
