    "karplus-strong-string": {
      "name": "Karplus-Strong String",
      "description": "A plucked string, played polyphonically. It is a body for a Voices node: tick **Polyphonic** on its Node tab to make it one, wire MIDI into its `midi` input, and every note plucks its own string, tuned to the note.\n\n- `damping` (0 to 1) darkens the string: the upper harmonics die away sooner than the fundamental, and high notes ring shorter than low ones, as on a real string. 0 is a bright, metallic wire.\n- `decay` is how long a held note rings, in seconds, before it has faded by 60 dB (with damping, high notes fade sooner).\n- `release` is the same for the time after the note is let go: short mutes the string like a lifted finger; set it to `decay` to let every note ring on like a harp.\n- `tone` (Hz) is the brightness of the pluck itself: low for a soft, thumb-like pluck, high for a hard pick.\n- `level` (dB) is how hard the string is plucked; each note's velocity scales it further.\n- `out` is the string's sound, mono.\n\nInside: a Voice node gives each note's frequency, trigger, gate, and velocity. On every trigger an ADSR opens for exactly one period of the note and lets through a burst of white Noise, scaled by velocity and softened by a lowpass Biquad (`tone`). The burst goes into a feedback Comb whose delay is one period, so it recirculates and rings at the note's pitch (the Karplus-Strong algorithm), while the Comb's damping lowpass, inside the loop, takes a little treble off on every pass. The Ring time row works out the feedback: a Switch picks `decay` while the gate is held and `release` after, and −60 dB divided by the number of periods in that time, as a gain, is what each pass keeps. The Tuning rows subtract the delay the damping filter adds (its phase at the note's frequency, from an atan2) from the period, which keeps the string in tune at any damping. A DC Block removes the offset a burst can leave circulating.",
      "version": 1,
      "author": "Audio Constructor",
      "tags": [
        "synth",
        "instrument",
        "string",
        "pluck",
        "physical model",
        "polyphonic"
      ],
      "source": "shipped:karplus-strong-string",
      "inputs": [
        {
          "name": "damping",
          "type": "float",
          "default": 0.2,
          "range": [
            0.0,
            1.0
          ],
          "targets": [
            "7:damping",
            "12:b",
            "16:in"
          ]
        },
        {
          "name": "decay",
          "type": "float",
          "unit": "seconds",
          "default": 4.0,
          "range": [
            0.1,
            20.0
          ],
          "targets": [
            "9:b"
          ]
        },
        {
          "name": "release",
          "type": "float",
          "unit": "seconds",
          "default": 0.5,
          "range": [
            0.05,
            20.0
          ],
          "targets": [
            "9:a"
          ]
        },
        {
          "name": "tone",
          "type": "float",
          "unit": "hz",
          "default": 8000.0,
          "range": [
            200.0,
            20000.0
          ],
          "targets": [
            "6:cutoff"
          ]
        },
        {
          "name": "level",
          "type": "float",
          "unit": "db",
          "default": 0.0,
          "range": [
            -60.0,
            12.0
          ],
          "targets": [
            "2:gain"
          ]
        }
      ],
      "outputs": [
        {
          "name": "out",
          "type": "audio",
          "source": "8:out"
        }
      ],
      "graph": {
        "nodes": [
          {
            "id": "1",
            "kind": "voice",
            "ui": {
              "pos": [
                0.0,
                0.0
              ]
            }
          },
          {
            "id": "2",
            "kind": "noise",
